{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>The region of Argob.</b> We translate it בֵּית פֶּלֶךְ טְרָכוֹנָא, and I saw the Jerusalem Targum in the scroll of Esther calling it פָּלָטִין טְרָכוֹנִין — I learned that חֶבֶל אַרְגּוֹב הִפַּרְכִיָּא means the palace of a king, that is, that the kingdom is called by its name; and likewise ״אֶת הָאַרְגּוֹב דִּמְלָכִים״ (II Kings 15:25) — near the palace of the king Pekah son of Remaliah killed Pekahiah son of Menahem — I learned that thus the name of the palatial district is called."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:47.478437178Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}